This study adopted a number of different insampled methods and manual curation to generate a partial genome sequence with a full-length viral genome of 86.3%.
We cannot rule out the possibility that pangolin is one of the intermediate animal nutrients of SARS-CoV-2.
However, there is currently no evidence in support of the direct pangolin origin of SARS-CoV-2 due to the sequence variety between SARS-CoV-2 and pangolin SARS-CoV-2-related beta-CoVs.
