The group stressed that the lack of resources or health insurance should never be used as a justification for differentiation towards a specific group.
Experts emphasised that every person, including people with disabilities, minority groups, older people, internally displaced people, homeless, people living in extremely poor conditions, people living in distress, as well as refugees and other unspecified groups in need of government assistance, have the right to health.
